Given limited edit size, maybe easier: we can rely on the browser's tab order and just detect when we are leaving the modal via focusout? Actually the enforceFocus listener already returns focus to modal when focus leaves. To implement wrapping, we could instead of returning focus to modal, we could check if the relatedTarget is null (i.e., focus went to browser chrome) and then decide to focus first or last based on shiftKey? However, the observed behavior shows focus moved to the modal itself (due to enforceFocus). So we need to intervene earlier.

